# Ignore everything by default
*

# Except these root files
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!.gitignore
!.gitleaksignore
!.env.ci
!docker-compose.yml
!archivebox.Dockerfile
!catallenya.png

# Except these folders (include everything inside)
!audit/
!caddy/
!changedetection/
!cloudflared/
!host/
!rclone/
!ntfy/
!restic/
!sanoid/
!systemd/
!.github/
!immich/
!tailscale/

# Explicit exclude audit logs
!audit/audit.sh

# Docs are per-file: docs/remote-luks-unlock.md is host-local ON PURPOSE (it is a
# recovery runbook naming real hosts and slots) and must never gain a `**` here.
!docs/
!docs/intake-playbook.md

# Explicit includes inside restic folder — per-file, NOT `**`. A `**` allowlist
# auto-tracks whatever lands in the directory later, and these hold the backup
# credentials' neighbours: restic/backup/creds.env or restic/staleness/token would
# have been swept up by `git add -A` into a PUBLIC repo. Same reasoning as
# capture/ below. restic.pwd stays ignored by the default `*` deny.
!restic/backup/
!restic/backup/restic.backup.service
!restic/backup/restic.backup.sh
!restic/backup/restic.backup.timer
!restic/check/
!restic/check/restic.check-data.timer
!restic/check/restic.check-subset.timer
!restic/check/restic.check.sh
!restic/check/restic.check@.service
!restic/check/instance-subset.conf
!restic/check/instance-data.conf
!restic/forget/
!restic/forget/restic.forget.service
!restic/forget/restic.forget.sh
!restic/forget/restic.forget.timer
!restic/misc/
!restic/misc/restic.restore.sh
!restic/misc/restic.snapshots.sh
!restic/misc/restic.unlock.sh
!restic/misc/restic.locks.sh
!restic/staleness/
!restic/staleness/restic.staleness.service
!restic/staleness/restic.staleness.sh
!restic/staleness/restic.staleness.timer
!restic/restic.conf

# Explicit includes inside .github — per-file. A `**` here would track a
# .github/workflows/secrets.env on sight.
!.github/workflows/
!.github/workflows/ci.yml
!.github/dependabot.yml

# Explicit includes inside caddy and cloudflared subfolders
!caddy/Caddyfile
!cloudflared/cloudflared.md

# Immich Public Proxy config (non-secret, stack-defining; mirrors caddy/Caddyfile).
# The container bind-mounts this file read-only, so it must exist on disk before
# `up` — track it so the service is reproducible from the repo.
!immich-public-proxy/
!immich-public-proxy/config.json

# Explicit includes notification scripts — per-file. The `ntfy/.env` re-deny below
# used to be the only guard, which shows the exposure was known; it just named one
# filename. ntfy/api-token.txt would still have been committed.
!changedetection/changedetection.health.sh
!host/disk.sh
!ntfy/system-ntfy.sh
!ntfy/system-ntfy@.service
!systemd/heartbeat.sh
ntfy/.env

# Explicit includes systemd services — per-file. A `**` here would track a
# systemd/id_rsa on sight.
!host/catallenya.sh
!changedetection/changedetection.health.service
!changedetection/changedetection.health.timer
!host/disk.service
!host/disk.timer
!immich/immich.fix-rotations.service
!immich/immich.fix-rotations.timer
!systemd/install.sh
!systemd/README.md
!systemd/systemd.md
!host/zpool.scrub.service
!host/zpool.scrub.timer
!systemd/catallenya.heartbeat.service
!systemd/catallenya.heartbeat.timer
# The job factory. Per-file, never !systemd/policy/** — a glob would auto-track
# whatever lands there later, and this repo is public.
!systemd/policy/
!systemd/policy/10-base.conf
!systemd/policy/10-base-timer.conf
!systemd/policy/20-scheduled.conf
!systemd/policy/20-monitor.conf
!systemd/policy/20-adhoc.conf
!systemd/policy/30-intake.conf
!systemd/policy/30-restic.conf
!systemd/tests/
!systemd/tests/run.sh
# systemd/state/ is deliberately absent: completion stamps are runtime state,
# recreated by install.sh and refreshed by every successful run.

# Explicit includes inside tailscale folder
# (tailscale/data + tailscale/tmp hold runtime state and stay ignored by the default `*` deny)
# Per-file, and this is the sharpest one: `tailscale/initrd-identity/tailscaled.state`
# is the persistent tailnet NODE KEY baked into every initramfs. Under a `**` a debug
# copy landing beside the generator script would have been published.
!tailscale/initrd-identity/
!tailscale/initrd-identity/generate-initrd-state.sh
!tailscale/initrd-identity/wire-initrd-state.sh
!tailscale/initramfs-hooks/
!tailscale/initramfs-hooks/initrd-tailscale-state

# Explicit includes inside immich folder
# (raw photo data + .immich_api_key stay ignored by the default `*` deny)
!immich/scripts/
!immich/scripts/immich.conf
!immich/scripts/immich.lib.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.validate.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.find-junk.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.verify-junk.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.delete.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.restore.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.fix-dates.scan.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.fix-dates.verify.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.fix-dates.apply.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.fix-rotations.sh
!immich/scripts/immich.fix-rotations.daily.sh
!immich/scripts/README.md

# Explicit includes inside documents folder — CODE ONLY, per-file, no ** globs
# (same reasoning as capture/ below: a `**` allowlist silently auto-tracks whatever
# lands in the directory later, and this is a public repo).
# pigeonhole/intake-state/ is runtime state — proposals, approval markers, rasterised
# scratch — and stays ignored by the default `*` deny. The document CORPUS is not
# here at all: it lives in syncthing/data/master/documents, which the top-level `*`
# keeps out of git entirely (personal IDs, medical, financial).
!pigeonhole/
!pigeonhole/README.md
!pigeonhole/scripts/
!pigeonhole/scripts/pigeonhole.lib.sh
!pigeonhole/scripts/pigeonhole.vocab.json
!pigeonhole/scripts/pigeonhole.triage.sh
!pigeonhole/scripts/pigeonhole.apply.sh
!pigeonhole/scripts/pigeonhole.sweep.sh
!pigeonhole/tests/
!pigeonhole/tests/run.sh
!pigeonhole/systemd/
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.triage.path
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.triage.service
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.apply.path
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.apply.service
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.backstop.timer
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.sweep.service
!pigeonhole/systemd/pigeonhole.sweep.timer

# The documents approve/discard container — CODE ONLY, same per-file discipline.
!pigeonhole/approve/
!pigeonhole/approve/Dockerfile
!pigeonhole/approve/.dockerignore
!pigeonhole/approve/src/
!pigeonhole/approve/src/server.ts

# Explicit includes inside capture folder — CODE/CONFIG ONLY, never data.
# afterimage/data/ holds uploaded screenshots (whatever was on screen at capture) plus
# pending events; the default `*` deny is what keeps it out of git. Do NOT add a
# blanket `!capture/**` — same reasoning as syncthing/immich above.
#
# Every file is listed individually, and directory globs (`!afterimage/src/**`) are
# deliberately NOT used: this is a public repo, and a `**` allowlist silently
# auto-tracks whatever lands in that directory later. The earlier glob form would
# have committed afterimage/scripts/.env or afterimage/client/id_rsa on sight. Adding a
# file here is one line; the alternative is a leak with no review step.
!afterimage/
!afterimage/.gitignore
!afterimage/.dockerignore
!afterimage/Dockerfile
!afterimage/OPERATIONS.md
!afterimage/README.md
!afterimage/src/
!afterimage/src/server.ts
!afterimage/scripts/
!afterimage/scripts/afterimage.lib.sh
!afterimage/scripts/afterimage.triage.sh
!afterimage/scripts/afterimage.sweep.sh
!afterimage/scripts/render_ics.py
!afterimage/systemd/
!afterimage/systemd/afterimage.triage.path
!afterimage/systemd/afterimage.triage.service
!afterimage/systemd/afterimage.sweep.service
!afterimage/systemd/afterimage.sweep.timer
!afterimage/client/
!afterimage/client/afterimage.sh
!afterimage/tests/
!afterimage/tests/run.sh

# Explicit includes inside the shared AI layer. Same per-file discipline as capture
# above — no `**` globs, so a stray key or scratch file landing in ai/ stays untracked
# until someone adds a line here on purpose.
!ai/
!ai/README.md
!ai/scripts/
!ai/scripts/ai.lib.sh
!ai/tests/
!ai/tests/run.sh
!ai/tests/sink.py

# Explicit includes inside the liquidroom pipeline — CODE ONLY, same per-file
# discipline. liquidroom/state/ (work spool + ~1 GB model cache) stays under the
# default `*` deny, as does anything else that lands here uninvited.
!liquidroom/
!liquidroom/.dockerignore
!liquidroom/Dockerfile
!liquidroom/OPERATIONS.md
!liquidroom/README.md
!liquidroom/entrypoint.sh
!liquidroom/process.py
!liquidroom/uninstall.sh
!liquidroom/scripts/
!liquidroom/scripts/liquidroom.lib.sh
!liquidroom/scripts/liquidroom.triage.sh
!liquidroom/scripts/models.sh
!liquidroom/systemd/
!liquidroom/systemd/liquidroom.triage.path
!liquidroom/systemd/liquidroom.triage.service
!liquidroom/tests/
!liquidroom/tests/run.sh
